From: Project Luma <builds@project-luma.local>
Subject: [PATCH] luma: keep the status cluster on the right edge

Pinning the gap before the status cluster seated the live extension
island against the clock, but it also applied to a shelf carrying only
the dock and the clock, where that gap is the only one there is and the
slack inside it is what holds the cluster against the right edge. The
clock moved to the middle of the shelf and only returned once a second
island appeared to take the slack.

diff --git a/js/ui/mediaSelection.js b/js/ui/mediaSelection.js
--- a/js/ui/mediaSelection.js
+++ b/js/ui/mediaSelection.js
@@ -52,9 +52,22 @@
     // instead, which is why it read as floating loose between the dock and the
     // clock rather than belonging to the clock. Pinning by position covers the
     // media island exactly as before and anything else that lands there.
-    const beforeStatus = children.indexOf(status) - 1;
+    const mediaPair = children.findIndex((child, index) =>
+        child === media && children[index + 1] === status);
     const gaps = children.slice(0, -1);
-    const flexible = gaps.length - (beforeStatus >= 0 ? 1 : 0);
-    return gaps.map((_child, index) => index === beforeStatus
+    // Pinning the gap before the status cluster is what keeps a live extension
+    // island against the clock. But on a shelf holding only the dock and the
+    // clock that same gap is the only thing there is, and the slack inside it
+    // is what carries the cluster to the right edge of the screen -- pinning it
+    // tight left the clock sitting next to the dock in the middle of the shelf.
+    // So it is only pinned when some earlier gap can take the slack instead.
+    // The media island keeps its own pin either way: the allocation treats a
+    // lone media-and-status pair as right-anchored already, so it needs no
+    // slack of its own.
+    const pinned = mediaPair >= 0
+        ? mediaPair
+        : (gaps.length > 1 ? children.indexOf(status) - 1 : -1);
+    const flexible = gaps.length - (pinned >= 0 ? 1 : 0);
+    return gaps.map((_child, index) => index === pinned
         ? gap : gap + (flexible ? spare / flexible : 0));
 }
